From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0144-global-atom-cas-32.patch

Source: 0144-global-atom-cas-32.patch
shader_recompiler: implement 32-bit global ATOM.CAS

compute shader using it failed to build (FINAL FANTASY RESONANCE there).

ATOM.CAS Rd, [Ra + imm], Rb compares the word with Rb, stores Rb+1 on a match and returns
the old word. Adds GlobalAtomicCompareExchange32 and StorageAtomicCompareExchange32, the
global-to-storage step with both operands, SPIR-V OpAtomicCompareExchange and GLSL
atomicCompSwap. GLASM, 64-bit CAS, ATOMS.CAS and SUATOM.CAS still throw.

META_TABLE and NUM_ARGS were sized by hand (539 here); they are sized by NUM_OPCODES now.

Changed from the PR: our routing of untracked global atomics is a different one
(global_atomic_funcs, define_body with three callback arguments), so the routed CAS is
written against it. Its address and operands arrive as Ids, as in our other global
atomics. As in the PR, a CAS with no matching buffer reports success, so that a guest
retry loop cannot spin for ever.

This is the Switch 1 style Maxwell path: the Ampere lowering emits no ATOM.CAS, so
Ocarina and Mario Kart World do not reach it through lowered programs.

